 wrapper signature and both forwarding paths are repaired statically.\n\nIntrinsic SO(3) mean adoption is prospective and limited to the active rotating-\noffset multi-master route, with unique convex/chart admission and unchanged\ndirect/zero-offset legacy semantics. Full orientation and offset derivatives,\nforce transfer, inverse/postcheck and nonlinear rotation dependency guards are\nrequired. The original coupling test module necessarily updates its old averaged-\nrotation expectation and adds objective tests; original tests/tolerances and the\nprotected backup remain preserved. Its hash has changed, and final identity must\nsay so. First focused objective check7passed/15deselected in1.88pytest seconds\n(evidence slice3-so3-mean-objectivity-3; process-wall3.8680314s). This is operator\nevidence only, not EP/reference/convergence acceptance. Nonauthor findings on\nmean-domain guards and snapshot/material assertions remain actionable in\nsupervisor_globalization_review.md and supervisor_findings.md.\n\r\nSixth run (160-turn delta) closed the unblock-and-deliver outcome and saved\r\nits handoff. The recover_initial_load_factor wrapper TypeError is fixed and\r\nexercised: _solve_static_displacement_control_block accepts the flag,\r\nincludes it in checkpoint_path and forwards it at both delegation sites;\r\nsplit-restart coverage passes both routes (slice3-so3-split-restart-1,\r\n17.39s). The adopted objective intrinsic SO(3) mean is implemented and\r\nverified on the active rotating-offset multi-master route: Karcher\r\nfixed-point _so3_weighted_mean with exact single-master/identical-rotation\r\nlimits and refusal guards, connected through slave orientation, full\r\njacobian (M = sum G_i P_i), per-master reduce_force covectors, FD-based\r\ngeometric tangent, force transfer, inverse/restart, postcheck and the\r\ndownstream multi-master rotation guard; direct/zero-offset legacy is\r\nbit-identical. The supervisor_objectivity_review.md moment-defect\r\ndiscriminator