gression of this new DC loop. Actual measured\npasses listed above remain evidence; current full targets are unverified.\nNonauthor integrated review confirms the map's core adjoint/Hessian integration,\nbut convex/chart guards and snapshot/history assertions remain blocking.\n\nAstra now performs the narrow final reconciliation of its reserved convex/chart\ncontract and independent acceptance assertions, plus the exact two-master mean\nformula needed to remove iterative-mean precision noise. This retains Mistral's\ncentral algorithm/integration authorship. Direct work is justified by coupling\nto scientific acceptance and repeated source-versus-handoff discrepancies;\nturn exhaustion alone is not the reason. Preserve the handed-back candidate in\ncandidate-identities/before-final-reconciliation. No numerical allowance renews:\nledger1876.2980378000066s,1723.7019621999934s remain, including900s final reserve.\nThe author's450s allocation is closed; task-owned acceptance checks use only the\nremaining original3600s budget. Retirement/release/public success semantics stand.\n\nAstra final reconciliation (prospective): two-master intrinsic means use their\nunique shortest geodesic for relative rotation below pi; this sharper uniqueness\ncondition supersedes a conservative pi/4 anchor restriction for TWO masters.\nFor larger supports, all inputs and the returned mean must lie in the declared\nopen pi/4 anchor ball. Multi-master input/output vectors stay inside the principal\nchart, including identical inputs. Accepted near-unit weights are normalized only\ninside the scale-invariant mean equation/differential. Physical translation uses\noriginal partition weights and the correction subtracts the original linear lever.\nThese admission/algorithm decisions precede new FE evidence and change no load,\nmaterial, reference, scientific tolerance or success definition.\nSnapshot assertions now audit actual linear constraints after inverse mapping,\ncompare deep preimages of st