{"id": "effect-661afd92-dcab-565d-8a11-5ccb2195bfe7", "sessionId": "3290534b-2fa0-0d5b-1a6c-5caaf888f672", "turnId": "turn-efff736df4afd6e2b448c337e3fb4175", "createdAt": 1792351783425, "updatedAt": 1792351783553, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.bash", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.bash", "display": {"summary": "bash: cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/supervisor-domain-dc-full-1/ && echo === && head -50 supervisor_dc_review.md 2>/dev/null && echo ===FIND=== && tail -80 supervisor_findings.md", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Running", "message": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/supervisor-domain-dc-full-1/ && echo === && head -50 supervisor_dc_review.md 2>/dev/null && echo ===FIND=== && tail -80 supervisor_findings.md", "settledVerb": "Ran", "settledMessage": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/supervisor-domain-dc-full-1/ && echo === && head -50 supervisor_dc_review.md 2>/dev/null && echo ===FIND=== && tail -80 supervisor_findings.md", "statusText": "Running command"}, "kind": "shell", "input": {"command": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/supervisor-domain-dc-full-1/ && echo === && head -50 supervisor_dc_review.md 2>/dev/null && echo ===FIND=== && tail -80 supervisor_findings.md"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"stdout": "preflight.json\npreflight_stderr.txt\npreflight_stdout.txt\nreceipt.json\nstderr.txt\nstdout.txt\n===\n# Independent DC lifecycle and continuation-test review\n\nStatic review of the in-progress owner edits, 2026-10-18. No imports, numerical\nsolves, pytest, product/test edits or additional workers. Mistral retains\nimplementation and numerical-execution ownership. Source was being edited during\nreview; transient incomplete indentation was not treated as a final defect.\nLine numbers identify the inspected version and may move.\n\n## Concrete product findings\n\n### DC1 — P1: zero control span can retry forever\n\nnonlinear_static.py:3961 computes min_control_subincrement from\nabs(target_increment)/(num_steps*256). At 4204–4217 a failed attempt is retried\nwhen half the attempted remaining span is >= that minimum. When the requested\ntarget equals the initial controlled displacement, both values are zero. The\ncondition remains true while attempt_fraction repeatedly halves, even after it\nunderflows to zero; every retry solves the same target with no progress.\n\nReachable example: ordinary finite DC restart at its current controlled target,\nno contact, rotating MPC, max_iterations=1. The helper starts lambda at zero.\nThe first Newton correction can recover the prior equilibrium lambda, but the\none-iteration loop ends before reevaluating convergence, reports the iteration\nlimit, rolls lambda back to zero and retries. The zero-span cutback condition\nnever terminates. This is independent of whether the physical state itself is\nalready valid at its known previous lambda.\n\nRequire strictly positive finite attempted span and representable target\nprogress before subdivision, with an explicit bounded minimum. A zero-span\nrequest can run its bounded Newton attempt but must retain a finite failure\nexit if it cannot converge. Do not rely on an external timeout to terminate the\nloop. Add a focused zero-span restart/forced-iteration-limit regression; it can\nuse a controlled fake assembler/factorization to verify bounded attempts.\n\n### DC2 — P2: per-step iteration counts accumulate across accepted subdivisions\n\nstep_iterations is initialized once per scheduled milestone at 3981 and\nincremented after each attempt at 4172. Every accepted subincrement publishes\nthat same cumulative count in NonlinearStaticStep and history around 4314/4331.\nIf the first accepted subincrement uses a iterations and the next b, their\nrecords report a and a+b. Summing records double-counts a even though the\nseparate total_iterations counter increments correctly per actual iteration.\n\nReset the per-published-increment iteration accumulator after acceptance (or at\nthe start of the next publication interval). Keep failed-attempt counts and\nscheduled-milestone totals in explicitly cumulative fields if desired. Preserve\nall failed-attempt work in the solve-wide total and evidence. The similarly\ncumulative attempts/cutbacks fields should state their scope, rather than\nimplicitly appearing to describe only that accepted subincrement.\n\n===FIND===\nParent single direct check supervisor-dc-direct-globalized-1 failed in4.519s\nBEFORE mechanics: the public driver passes recover_initial_load_factor into\nnonlinear_performance._solve_static_displacement_control_block, whose signature\ndoes not accept/forward it. Repair that shared wrapper (inside owned five files),\nthen rerun the single -x case with trace/progress rather than broad sweeps. Tests\nand globalization changes remain unverified. Five wrappers have ended without\nhandoff; provide a concrete end-to-end candidate and saved handoff this time,\nwith realistic sustained turn capacity rather than restarting investigation.\n\nFrame-convention clarification for the rigid-spin probe: in PHYSICAL current\npositions x_b=sum(w_i*x_i)+R_mean*r0. In DISPLACEMENTS it is\nu_b=sum(w_i*u_i)+(R_mean-I)*r0 (assuming X_b=sum(w_i*X_i)+r0).\nThe checkpoint's physical-x formula with (R-I) omitted that initial offset.\nSuperpose rigid rotation using u_i^Q=Q*(X_i+u_i)-X_i, not Q*u_i alone. A direct\ncontrol must pass at roundoff; the noncommuting interp failure should match D.\n\nEarly helper review (_so3_mean_block.py): implicit G_i formula agrees with\ndelta psi_i=Jl(psi_i)^-1 Rm.T*(delta alpha_i-delta alpha_m). However normpsi<pi\nand detB>0 do NOT enforce the adopted unique local convex mean: equal masters\nRx(+pi/2),Rx(-pi/2) admit two means I andRx(pi), and pass those checks. Restrict\nthe supported local convex neighborhood explicitly (e.g. each relative rotation\nstrictly withinpi/2, with boundary refusal), and handle the absolute principal\nrotation-vector mean chart boundary. Exact-identical shortcut at raw theta>pi\nwould otherwise differ discontinuously from the principal-log perturbed path.\nKeep direct legacy behavior, but do not claim unsupported active-interp chart\ncontinuation. Add focused ambiguous/chart refusal regression. No new FE sweep.\n\nIndependent updated EP test review (full report supervisor_globalization_review.md\nforthcoming): apply_kinematics(to_linear_displacement(u)) is an ambient inverse\nidentity for ANY bad slave perturbation, so it is NOT manifold membership.\nRun constraint_residual_summary(model, to_linear_displacement(snapshot_u)) or\nexplicit physical relations at existing tolerances for EVERY snapshot. Preserve\ndeep pre-reconstruction copies, not aliased state references, for immutability.\nThe resumed snapshots start AFTER-.10; current material comparison loop includes\n-.10 and calls _snapshot_at_control(resumed,-.10), which must fail. Compare split\nstate using half vs full split, then only later resumed milestone snapshots.\n\nMean-domain resolution from independent review: adopt a conservative equivariant\nanchor ball around the FIRST master, strict radiuspi/4, for active multi-master\nmeans. All master orientations AND returned mean must be inside that ball;\ndistances use Log(R_first.T R_i), invariant under common left rotation. This\ngives an explicit convex local domain instead of treating detB as uniqueness.\nCheck the symmetric B part is positive definite before solve. Enforce supported\nabsolute principal rotation-vector chart for multi-master inputs/mean BEFORE\nthe identical shortcut (reject boundary/out-of-chart); preserve one-master\ndirect legacy handling separately. Add the small noncommuting admissible\nrigid-spin case and ambiguous/chart refusal cases. Required planar benchmark\nneighbor rotations are inside this local domain; actual EP states still need\nmeasurement. No arbitrary chart continuation claim.\n\nImmediate SO3 FD failure diagnosis: debug_so3_map.py computes J at the MANUALLY\nmodified u_lin, but FD at T@(old q +/- dq)+u0. Those are DIFFERENT centers.\n_interp_map_with_distinct_master_rotations explicitly says its manual state is\nnot inimageT (it even changes fixed root rotations); this cannot test du/dq.\nUse a single admissible q (e.g. seeded independent coordinates in[-.15,.15]) and\nu_lin=T@q+u0 for BOTH J andFD, ensuring distinct noncommuting free rotations.\nDo not repair correct mean G_i based on this mismatched-state comparison.\nThe finite rigid-spin test also updates shared master nodes repeatedly while\nlooping couplings; transform each unique master ONCE from original state, then\nrebuild all slave linear rows. Repeated Q applications are a fixture defect.\n\nExisting original coupling test module has been edited outside the prior\nnew-test-only boundary. Astra prospectively admits the NECESSARY updates to its\nold weighted-rotation expectation to reflect the adopted objective mean, while\npreserving every original test and tolerance and protected backup. New objective\nregressions may remain there (the final selection includes this module). Use an\nindependent two-master geodesic reference R1*Exp(w2*Log(R1.T*R2)), not a call to\nthe production mean as the sole oracle; independent FD/spatial wrench tests also\nremain. Do not edit the original work-conjugate module. Record original-module\nchanges explicitly; the final manifest must not claim its hash unchanged.\n\nPerformance/precision discriminant after full coupling module240s timeout:\nall relevant edge interpolations have TWO masters. Their intrinsic mean has\nthe exact closed form Rm=R1*Exp(t*Log(R1.T*R2)), t=w2/(w1+w2). It satisfies\nthe adopted Karcher equation, keeps the same implicit G_i derivation and avoids\niteration stopping noise1e-14 being amplified by stiff EA/short elements, as\nwell as repeated fixed-point work inside Hessian probes. This is a compatible\ninternal algorithm, not a load/reference/tolerance fit. Consider this exact\ntwo-master branch before repeating a slow unchanged large-angle solve. Retain\nthe direct analytic lever-arm Hessian where possible; no unmeasured speed claim.\n", "stderr": "", "output": "", "truncated": false}, "outputText": "preflight.json\npreflight_stderr.txt\npreflight_stdout.txt\nreceipt.json\nstderr.txt\nstdout.txt\n===\n# Independent DC lifecycle and continuation-test review\n\nStatic review of the in-progress owner edits, 2026-10-18. No imports, numerical\nsolves, pytest, product/test edits or additional workers. Mistral retains\nimplementation and numerical-execution ownership. Source was being edited during\nreview; transient incomplete indentation was not treated as a final defect.\nLine numbers identify the inspected version and may move.\n\n## Concrete product findings\n\n### DC1 — P1: zero control span can retry forever\n\nnonlinear_static.py:3961 computes min_control_subincrement from\nabs(target_increment)/(num_steps*256). At 4204–4217 a failed attempt is retried\nwhen half the attempted remaining span is >= that minimum. When the requested\ntarget equals the initial controlled displacement, both values are zero. The\ncondition remains true while attempt_fraction repeatedly halves, even after it\nunderflows to zero; every retry solves the same target with no progress.\n\nReachable example: ordinary finite DC restart at its current controlled target,\nno contact, rotating MPC, max_iterations=1. The helper starts lambda at zero.\nThe first Newton correction can recover the prior equilibrium lambda, but the\none-iteration loop ends before reevaluating convergence, reports the iteration\nlimit, rolls lambda back to zero and retries. The zero-span cutback condition\nnever terminates. This is independent of whether the physical state itself is\nalready valid at its known previous lambda.\n\nRequire strictly positive finite attempted span and representable target\nprogress before subdivision, with an explicit bounded minimum. A zero-span\nrequest can run its bounded Newton attempt but must retain a finite failure\nexit if it cannot converge. Do not rely on an external timeout to terminate the\nloop. Add a focused zero-span restart/forced-iteration-limit regression; it can\nuse a controlled fake assembler/factorization to verify bounded attempts.\n\n### DC2 — P2: per-step iteration counts accumulate across accepted subdivisions\n\nstep_iterations is initialized once per scheduled milestone at 3981 and\nincremented after each attempt at 4172. Every accepted subincrement publishes\nthat same cumulative count in NonlinearStaticStep and history around 4314/4331.\nIf the first accepted subincrement uses a iterations and the next b, their\nrecords report a and a+b. Summing records double-counts a even though the\nseparate total_iterations counter increments correctly per actual iteration.\n\nReset the per-published-increment iteration accumulator after acceptance (or at\nthe start of the next publication interval). Keep failed-attempt counts and\nscheduled-milestone totals in explicitly cumulative fields if desired. Preserve\nall failed-attempt work in the solve-wide total and evidence. The similarly\ncumulative attempts/cutbacks fields should state their scope, rather than\nimplicitly appearing to describe only that accepted subincrement.\n\n===FIND===\nParent single direct check supervisor-dc-direct-globalized-1 failed in4.519s\nBEFORE mechanics: the public driver passes recover_initial_load_factor into\nnonlinear_performance._solve_static_displacement_control_block, whose signature\ndoes not accept/forward it. Repair that shared wrapper (inside owned five files),\nthen rerun the single -x case with trace/progress rather than broad sweeps. Tests\nand globalization changes remain unverified. Five wrappers have ended without\nhandoff; provide a concrete end-to-end candidate and saved handoff this time,\nwith realistic sustained turn capacity rather than restarting investigation.\n\nFrame-convention clarification for the rigid-spin probe: in PHYSICAL current\npositions x_b=sum(w_i*x_i)+R_mean*r0. In DISPLACEMENTS it is\nu_b=sum(w_i*u_i)+(R_mean-I)*r0 (assuming X_b=sum(w_i*X_i)+r0).\nThe checkpoint's physical-x formula with (R-I) omitted that initial offset.\nSuperpose rigid rotation using u_i^Q=Q*(X_i+u_i)-X_i, not Q*u_i alone. A direct\ncontrol must pass at roundoff; the noncommuting interp failure should match D.\n\nEarly helper review (_so3_mean_block.py): implicit G_i formula agrees with\ndelta psi_i=Jl(psi_i)^-1 Rm.T*(delta alpha_i-delta alpha_m). However normpsi<pi\nand detB>0 do NOT enforce the adopted unique local convex mean: equal masters\nRx(+pi/2),Rx(-pi/2) admit two means I andRx(pi), and pass those checks. Restrict\nthe supported local convex neighborhood explicitly (e.g. each relative rotation\nstrictly withinpi/2, with boundary refusal), and handle the absolute principal\nrotation-vector mean chart boundary. Exact-identical shortcut at raw theta>pi\nwould otherwise differ discontinuously from the principal-log perturbed path.\nKeep direct legacy behavior, but do not claim unsupported active-interp chart\ncontinuation. Add focused ambiguous/chart refusal regression. No new FE sweep.\n\nIndependent updated EP test review (full report supervisor_globalization_review.md\nforthcoming): apply_kinematics(to_linear_displacement(u)) is an ambient inverse\nidentity for ANY bad slave perturbation, so it is NOT manifold membership.\nRun constraint_residual_summary(model, to_linear_displacement(snapshot_u)) or\nexplicit physical relations at existing tolerances for EVERY snapshot. Preserve\ndeep pre-reconstruction copies, not aliased state references, for immutability.\nThe resumed snapshots start AFTER-.10; current material comparison loop includes\n-.10 and calls _snapshot_at_control(resumed,-.10), which must fail. Compare split\nstate using half vs full split, then only later resumed milestone snapshots.\n\nMean-domain resolution from independent review: adopt a conservative equivariant\nanchor ball around the FIRST master, strict radiuspi/4, for active multi-master\nmeans. All master orientations AND returned mean must be inside that ball;\ndistances use Log(R_first.T R_i), invariant under common left rotation. This\ngives an explicit convex local domain instead of treating detB as uniqueness.\nCheck the symmetric B part is positive definite before solve. Enforce supported\nabsolute principal rotation-vector chart for multi-master inputs/mean BEFORE\nthe identical shortcut (reject boundary/out-of-chart); preserve one-master\ndirect legacy handling separately. Add the small noncommuting admissible\nrigid-spin case and ambiguous/chart refusal cases. Required planar benchmark\nneighbor rotations are inside this local domain; actual EP states still need\nmeasurement. No arbitrary chart continuation claim.\n\nImmediate SO3 FD failure diagnosis: debug_so3_map.py computes J at the MANUALLY\nmodified u_lin, but FD at T@(old q +/- dq)+u0. Those are DIFFERENT centers.\n_interp_map_with_distinct_master_rotations explicitly says its manual state is\nnot inimageT (it even changes fixed root rotations); this cannot test du/dq.\nUse a single admissible q (e.g. seeded independent coordinates in[-.15,.15]) and\nu_lin=T@q+u0 for BOTH J andFD, ensuring distinct noncommuting free rotations.\nDo not repair correct mean G_i based on this mismatched-state comparison.\nThe finite rigid-spin test also updates shared master nodes repeatedly while\nlooping couplings; transform each unique master ONCE from original state, then\nrebuild all slave linear rows. Repeated Q applications are a fixture defect.\n\nExisting original coupling test module has been edited outside the prior\nnew-test-only boundary. Astra prospectively admits the NECESSARY updates to its\nold weighted-rotation expectation to reflect the adopted objective mean, while\npreserving every original test and tolerance and protected backup. New objective\nregressions may remain there (the final selection includes this module). Use an\nindependent two-master geodesic reference R1*Exp(w2*Log(R1.T*R2)), not a call to\nthe production mean as the sole oracle; independent FD/spatial wrench tests also\nremain. Do not edit the original work-conjugate module. Record original-module\nchanges explicitly; the final manifest must not claim its hash unchanged.\n\nPerformance/precision discriminant after full coupling module240s timeout:\nall relevant edge interpolations have TWO masters. Their intrinsic mean has\nthe exact closed form Rm=R1*Exp(t*Log(R1.T*R2)), t=w2/(w1+w2). It satisfies\nthe adopted Karcher equation, keeps the same implicit G_i derivation and avoids\niteration stopping noise1e-14 being amplified by stiff EA/short elements, as\nwell as repeated fixed-point work inside Hessian probes. This is a compatible\ninternal algorithm, not a load/reference/tolerance fit. Consider this exact\ntwo-master branch before repeating a slow unchanged large-angle solve. Retain\nthe direct analytic lever-arm Hessian where possible; no unmeasured speed claim.\n", "durationMs": 0.0, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && ls evidence/supervisor-domain-dc-full-1/ && echo === && head -50 supervisor_dc_review.md 2>/dev/null && echo ===FIND=== && tail -80 supervisor_findings.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "effect-27c79665-5529-5a08-b41a-c06e04b52fd5", "sessionId": "3290534b-2fa0-0d5b-1a6c-5caaf888f672", "turnId": "turn-efff736df4afd6e2b448c337e3fb4175", "createdAt": 1792351783453, "updatedAt": 1792351783583, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "file_system.bash", "detail": {"toolName": "file_system.bash", "display": {"summary": "bash: cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && cat product_execution_ceiling.json && echo === && cat product_execution_ceiling-before-final-repair.json 2>/dev/null && echo ===HARNESS=== && head -120 harness.py", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Running", "message": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && cat product_execution_ceiling.json && echo === && cat product_execution_ceiling-before-final-repair.json 2>/dev/null && echo ===HARNESS=== && head -120 harness.py", "settledVerb": "Ran", "settledMessage": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && cat product_execution_ceiling.json && echo === && cat product_execution_ceiling-before-final-repair.json 2>/dev/null && echo ===HARNESS=== && head -120 harness.py", "statusText": "Running command"}, "kind": "shell", "input": {"command": "cd \"C:/Github/ANYsolver/.development/nonlinear-master-slave-coupling-20261017\" && cat product_execution_ceiling.json && echo === && cat product_execution_ceiling-before-final-repair.json 2>/dev/null && echo ===HARNESS=== && head -120 harness.py"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"stdout": "{\r\n  \"active\": true,\r\n  \"allocation_seconds\": 220.0,\r\n  \"initial_used_seconds\": 2030.6258823000244,\r\n  \"reason\": \"same-owner focused final repair, no renewed overall authority\",\r\n  \"absolute_process_wall_ceiling_seconds\": 2250.6258823000244\r\n}===\n{\r\n  \"active\": false,\r\n  \"absolute_process_wall_ceiling_seconds\": 1936.0224586999684,\r\n  \"scope\": \"Remaining product repair continuation: original450s assignment, all charged attempts count; not renewed authority\",\r\n  \"closed_reason\": \"Implementation owner handed back; original overall task allowance and final reserve unchanged\"\r\n}===HARNESS===\n\"\"\"Slice 3 task harness: bounded, evidenced numerical execution.\n\nUsage (from anywhere):\n  <repo>/.venv/Scripts/python.exe harness.py --name ATTEMPT [--timeout 120]\n      [--cwd DIR] [--allow-reserve] [--hash-input PATH]... [--src-override DIR]\n      [--skip-preflight] -- CMD ARGS...\n\nRecords under evidence/<name>/:\n  receipt.json  command, cwd, selected-source identity + import-origin\n                verification, runtime record, exit/timeout status, precise\n                process-wall seconds, cumulative budget, named test counts\n  preflight.json  effective versions, import origins, threadpool, effective\n                numba DISABLE_JIT state\n  stdout.txt / stderr.txt  full streamed output (preserved on timeout and on\n                any harness exception)\n  running.json  live lock record (removed on completion)\n\nBudget ledger persists in budget.json (allowance 3600 s, final-verification\nreserve 900 s). Every attempt, including failures, timeouts and harness-side\nexceptions, is charged and recorded. One numerical child at a time is enforced\nwith a lock file. When --src-override is given it REPLACES the PYTHONPATH\nsource root (the candidate src is never added), and the receipt verifies the\nactual anysolver import origin against the selected root.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nTASK_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = TASK_DIR.parents[1]\nEVIDENCE = TASK_DIR / \"evidence\"\nBUDGET_FILE = TASK_DIR / \"budget.json\"\nLOCK_FILE = TASK_DIR / \"running.lock\"\nALLOWANCE = 3600.0\nRESERVE = 900.0\n\nIDENTITY_FILES = [\n    \"src/anysolver/corotational.py\",\n    \"src/anysolver/elements.py\",\n    \"src/anysolver/mesh_gen.py\",\n    \"src/anysolver/nonlinear_static.py\",\n    \"src/anysolver/nonlinear_performance.py\",\n    \"tests/test_corotational_work_conjugate.py\",\n    \"tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_coupling.py\",\n]\n\nCHILD_ENV = {\n    \"OMP_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n    \"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n    \"MKL_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n    \"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n    \"NUMBA_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n    \"NUMBA_DISABLE_JIT\": \"1\",\n    \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\": \"1\",\n    \"PYTHONHASHSEED\": \"0\",\n    \"PYTHONNOUSERSITE\": \"1\",\n    \"PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD\": \"1\",\n    \"ANYSOLVER_RUN_RETIRED_PROGRAMME_TESTS\": \"0\",\n}\n\nPREFLIGHT_CODE = r\"\"\"\nimport json, sys\ninfo = {\"python\": sys.version}\ntry:\n    import numpy, scipy\n    info[\"numpy\"] = numpy.__version__\n    info[\"scipy\"] = scipy.__version__\nexcept Exception as exc:\n    info[\"numpy_error\"] = repr(exc)\nfor name in (\"anysolver\", \"anymaterial\", \"anygeometry\", \"anymesher\", \"anyfileio\"):\n    try:\n        mod = __import__(name)\n        info[name] = {\n            \"version\": getattr(mod, \"__version__\", None),\n            \"origin\": getattr(mod, \"__file__\", None),\n        }\n    except Exception as exc:\n        info[name] = {\"error\": repr(exc)}\ntry:\n    import numba\n    info[\"numba\"] = numba.__version__\n    info[\"numba_disable_jit_effective\"] = bool(numba.config.DISABLE_JIT)\nexcept Exception as exc:\n    info[\"numba\"] = None\n    info[\"numba_error\"] = repr(exc)\ntry:\n    from threadpoolctl import threadpool_info\n    info[\"threadpools\"] = threadpool_info()\nexcept Exception:\n    info[\"threadpools\"] = \"unavailable\"\nprint(json.dumps(info))\n\"\"\"\n\n# Named pytest summary parsing: the terminal summary line lists categories in\n# any order (\"2 failed, 60 passed, 1 skipped\", \"60 passed\", \"3 error\", ...).\n_COUNT_CATEGORY = re.compile(r\"(\\d+) (passed|failed|skipped|error|errors|xfailed|xpassed|warning|warnings)\")\n\n\ndef sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(1 << 20), b\"\"):\n            h.update(chunk)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef load_budget() -> dict:\n    if BUDGET_FILE.exists():\n        with open(BUDGET_FILE, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            return json.load(fh)\n    return {\n", "stderr": "", "output": "", "truncated": false}, "outputText": "{\r\n  \"active\": true,\r\n  \"allocation_seconds\": 220.0,\r\n  \"initial_used_seconds\": 2030.6258823000244,\r\n  \"reason\": \"same-owner focused final repair, no renewed overall authority\",\r\n  \"absolute_process_wall_ceiling_seconds\": 2250.6258823000244\r\n}===\n{\r\n  \"active\": false,\r\n  \"absolute_process_wall_ceiling_seconds\": 1936.0224586999684,\r\n  \"scope\": \"Remaining product repair continuation: original450s assignment, all charged attempts count; not renewed authority\",\r\n  \"closed_reason\": \"Implementation owner handed back; original overall task allowance and final reserve unchanged\"\r\n}===HARNESS===\n\"\"\"Slice 3 task harness: bounded, evidenced numerical execution.\n\nUsage (from anywhere):\n  <repo>/.venv/Scripts/python.exe harness.py --name ATTEMPT [--timeout 120]\n      [--cwd DIR] [--allow-reserve] [--hash-input PATH]... [--src-override DIR]\n      [--skip-preflight] -- CMD ARGS...\n\nRecords under evidence/<name>/:\n  receipt.json  command, cwd, selected-source identity + import-origin\n                verification, runtime record, exit/timeout status, precise\n                process-wall seconds, cumulative budget, named test counts\n  preflight.json  effective versions, import origins, threadpool, effective\n                numba DISABLE_JIT state\n  stdout.txt / stderr.txt  full streamed output (preserved on timeout and on\n                any ha