in guards in `_so3_weighted_mean`: chart input, ambiguous geodesic, anchor ball, convergence, boundary, singular B. Keep the nonneg-weight and partition checks as ValueError? Those are input-contract errors (build-time), not state-domain — keep as ValueError. Actually the finite check too. The domain refusals that can legitimately arise from a trial STATE are: input chart, ambiguous geodesic (two-master relative rotation ≥ π−1e-6), anchor ball, non-convergence, mean boundary, singular B. I'll raise SO3MeanDomainError for those, subclassing ValueError so existing tests expecting ValueError still pass.\n\nIn nonlinear_static.py DC loop:\n1. Line search: wrap the trial evaluation (full_u(q_trial) + assembly + reduce_force) in try/except SO3MeanDomainError → treat trial as inadmissible: continue to next smaller alpha (merit_trial = inf effectively).\n2. After the line search (and for the no-line-search path), before committing `q += delta`, verify the candidate endpoint admissibility: `full_u(q + delta[:-1])` — but that's an extra kinematics evaluation per iteration (cheap relative to assembly). If it raises SO3MeanDomainError → failure_reason = \"trial_state_domain_refused\" (new classified reason), break → rollback path (discard candidate, q/lam restored). Then the subdivision logic: should domain refusal subdivide? A smaller control span gives a smaller Newton step, plausibly admissible. I'll make it subdivision-eligible like maximum_iterations_reached (bounded by cutback count), and if subdivision is exhausted → status stopped_at_limit with the classified reason recorded. Hmm, but brief says \"return classified failure after rollback\" — the rollback happens; the classified failure reason is recorded in the result. The status semantics: \"stopped_at_limit\" if steps else \"diverged\" — keep. The failure reason should be exposed. Let me check how failure_reason is exposed in the result... There's \"stop_reason\" in the probe output (\"minimum_control_step_reached\").