p full -0.20: `ValueError: interp_beam_shell_201: interpolated\n    SO(3) mean is outside the principal rotation-vector chart` raised from\n    `full_u(q_trial)` inside the DC residual line search\n    (nonlinear_static.py:4220 -> corotational.py:1248), aborting the whole\n    solve from an otherwise valid committed state.\n\n### Concrete diagnosis so far\n\n1. Interp abort mechanism is fully identified (traceback above): the line\n   search evaluates trial states `full_u(q_line_start + alpha*delta[:-1])`;\n   for alpha=1 (and possibly all 8 halvings) the trial master rotations can\n   leave the supported principal chart, `_so3_weighted_mean` raises a bare\n   ValueError and the exception propagates out of\n   `solve_static_nonlinear`, discarding a valid committed state. The\n   committed `q` itself is admissible (all previous `full_u(q)` succeeded),\n   so by continuity small alpha should be admissible; the defect is that\n   domain refusal is not treated as trial inadmissibility.\n2. Direct stop: the only per-accepted/per-iteration evidence\n   (ep-dc-limit-probe-2, ep-dc-step11-probe-1, ep-dc-block-probe-direct-1)\n   predates the current residual line search, so it is NOT current evidence\n   for the direct stop. It shows the pre-line-search pattern: steps 1-10\n   accept in 6-7 iterations (lam rising to 2.803 at ctrl -0.1667), then\n   accepted increments need 47/93/139/146 iterations with cutbacks while lam\n   passes a peak near 2.82 and descends to 2.668 at ctrl -0.18333; the\n   per-iteration trace at step 11 shows the reduced residual cycling\n   4e3..3e5 with lam oscillating 2.7..3.2 — a Newton limit cycle consistent\n   with plastic branch flip-flop plus full-step fallback. Current-source\n   per-accepted progress for the direct full target is the missing\n   discriminating measurement; one instrumented run is the next action.\n\n### Intended edits (bounded, compatible)\n\n1. `corotational.py`: add a typed `SO3MeanDomainError(ValueError)` raised by\n   the domain guards of `_so3_weighted_mean` (input chart, ambiguous\n   two-master geodesic, anchor-ball admission/convergence/boundary, mean\n   chart boundary, singular B). ValueError compatibility is retained; the\n   input-contract guards (finite, nonnegative, partition weights) stay plain\n   ValueError. No physics, chart, tolerance or admission change.\n2. `nonlinear_static.py` DC loop (rotating-MPC route only):\n   - line search: a trial whose `full_u`/assembly raises SO3MeanDomainError\n     is inadmissible — record merit +inf and continue halving; never commit\n     a refused trial and never mutate constitutive state on it (trial\n     states are already discarded).\n   - commit guard: before `q += delta`, if the candidate endpoint is\n     inadmissible (same typed error), do not commit; set a classified\n     failure reason (e.g. `trial_state_domain_refused`), roll back to the\n     attempt start (existing discard/restore path) and let the existing\n     bounded subdivision decide; when subdivision is exhausted the solve\n     returns the classified failure with the committed state preserved —\n     no abort, no invalid fallback step.\n   - direct-route globalization repair: decided from the instrumented run\n     below; candidate hypothesis is that the \"keep the full Newton step\n     when no line-search alpha improves\" fallback sustains the plastic\n     flip-flop cycle, and a compatible repair is to treat a no-improving-\n     step iteration as a failed attempt (rollback + bounded subdivision)\n     instead of committing a merit-increasing full step. To be confirmed\n     against the current-source measurement before editing.\n3. Focused regression in tests/test_nonlinear_beam_shell_slice3*.py:\n   trial refusal backtracks (or classified-fails) with preserved committed\n   state and no constitutive mutation on refused trials; uses a small\n   fixture/monkeypatched domain refusal, not a full-target solve.\n\n### Planned checks (within 220 s allocation)\n\