teration: I'll have the assemble wrapper increment a global counter, and the factorize wrapper logs the count since last factorize.\n\nAdditionally, to directly observe line-search alpha decisions, I could wrap `NonlinearRotatingMPCMap.apply_kinematics`... not needed; assembly counting suffices (each line-search trial does exactly one assembly with tangent=False).\n\nWait — actually the line search calls `_assemble_nonlinear_system(model, u_trial, ..., tangent=False, ...)`. The main loop calls with tangent=True (default? it passes corotational_tangent...). I can record the tangent flag per call to distinguish.\n\nLet me also catch the case where the solve raises (interp) — but this run is direct only.\n\nTimeout: 120s. Previous direct full run took ~88.75s with extra FD work; the limit probe direct full took... ep-dc-limit-probe-2 ran both direct and interp (\"full\" = both) and timed out at 120 — direct part finished (its output printed) then interp presumably hung. So direct alone is maybe 60-90s. With 40 max iterations (DC_MAX_ITER=40) vs the probe's earlier 25? The limit probe used max_iterations=40. OK ~60-90s expected.\n\nWrite the script now.", "summary": []}
