tes equal initial deep copy. That's the \"preserved state\" regression. \n\n   Two tests:\n   - test_dc_trial_domain_refusal_backtracks_and_preserves_state: inflate all solves ×1000 (enough to push trial master rotations past π). Assert: no exception; status stopped_at_limit; failure_reason == \"trial_state_domain_refused\"; displacements all zero; element states deep-equal to initial copy; control_cutbacks bounded (<= max).\n     Wait — need the model to actually have a rotating interp map with 2 masters and real chart guards. _build_coupled_cantilever(\"interpolated\"?) — check available coupling names in the slice3 test module. The zero-span test used \"eccentric\". Let me check the fixture builder.\n   - test_dc_line_search_no_improvement_classifies_and_rolls_back: growing force perturbation. Assert failure_reason == \"line_search_no_improvement\", status stopped_at_limit, zero displacements, states preserved.\n\n   Also keep the inflation factor: master rotations needed ≥ π. The small cantilever at target -0.01 m: rotations ~ small. Newton delta for 1 step: dq ~ 0.01-ish rotations ~0.01 rad. Inflate ×1000 → 10 rad > π. But delta also includes dlam and translations ×1000 — fine, trial is wild. But careful: the trial assembly at alpha=1 with wild u_trial — could crash inside element code (nonfinite, sqrt of negative, etc.) BEFORE the chart guard? full_u(q_trial) raises SO3MeanDomainError during apply_kinematics — BEFORE any assembly. The chart check happens in the mean computation inside apply_kinematics. With rotations ~10 rad, rotation_matrix_from_vector is fine (sin/cos), norm ≥ π → raise. Good — no element code runs. For alpha=0.5: 5 rad > π → also refused... all 8 alphas: alpha=2^-7=0.0078 × 10 rad = 0.078 rad < π → admissible! So trials 1..~5 refused, smaller admissible. any_trial_admissible=True → constraint unsatisfied (iteration 1) → keep full step → commit guard: full_u(q+delta) raises → trial_state_domain_refused → rollback → subdivide. Attempt 2: same