em adding growing force: force = force + n * 1e6 * e_unit? The residual scale: the eccentric cantilever with 100 N load; reduced residual ~100. Adding 1e6*n to one dof → residual jumps ~1e6*n → merit strictly increasing with call count → no trial improves. But careful: the convergence check at iteration 2 top: residual huge → not converged. Constraint: after iteration 1's full step, constraint ≈ 0 → guard triggers. \n\nBut wait — iteration 1: does the line search accept some alpha? merit_current at iter 1 = 0 + constraint/(tol*target_scale) — huge. Trials: merit_trial = res_trial/(tol*ref) + constraint_trial/(tol*target_scale). With perturbation n growing: first trial (alpha=1): res includes perturbation from call #2 (if wrapper counts across all calls). res_trial ~1e6 → merit ~1e6/(1e-8*ref). ref ~ reduced norm of proportional load ~100-ish → 1e6/1e-6 = 1e12. merit_current ~ span/(1e-8*0.001?) — target small, target_scale maybe max(|target|,1)=1? If target = -0.01, target_scale could be 1.0 or 0.01... merit_current ~ 0.01/(1e-8*1) = 1e6. merit_trial 1e12 >> 1e6 → fails. All alphas fail → constraint unsatisfied → keep full step → commit. Iteration 2: constraint ~0 → satisfied; merit_current = res(call#3)/(1e-8*ref) ~ 2e12...; trials: res(call#4) > res(call#3) → all fail → line_search_no_improvement. \n\nAlso need adaptive_control_subdivision active — it's on for the rotating route (the zero-span test shows subdivision machinery active; adaptive_control_subdivision = (rotating map present and ...?) line 3991: `adaptive_control_subdivision = (` — check the condition quickly.\n\nAlso max_iterations: set 40 (default DC) or small like 5 — with the no-improvement classification, the attempt fails at iteration 2, so max_iterations=5 is fine and bounds worst-case behavior.\n\nFor the domain-refusal test: interp route nx=2, ny=1. Displacement control at a shell node uz target -0.01, 1 step, max_iterations=5, tolerance 1e-8. Inflation factor: need master rotations ≥ π at alpha=1 trial. The true Newton step for -0.01 target: rotations ~0.01-0.05 rad. Inflate ×1000 → 10-50 rad > π. But also need SOME smaller alpha admissible so any_trial_admissible=True... actually not required — if ALL trials refused → any_trial_admissible=False → trial_state_domain_refused at B5 directly (constraint unsatisfied? B5 first checks `not any_trial_admissible` → refused regardless of constraint). Either path gives the same failure reason. Good.\n\nBut wait: with inflation ×1000, alpha=2^-7=0.0078 → 0.078-0.39 rad < π → admissible → any_trial_admissible=True → constraint unsatisfied → keep full step → commit guard → full_u(q+delta) raises → trial_state_domain_refused. Same reason. \n\nAlso the wrapper must inflate only the DC augmented factorization — factorize is called elsewhere? Within this solve, factorize is called in the DC loop (aug) and possibly in equilibration/initialization? With no initial fields, probably only the DC loop. The wrapper counts calls; inflate all — fine.\n\nOne catch: my wrapper returns delta*1000 — the augmented system solve returns [dq, dlam]; inflating dlam ×1000 too. Fine.\n\nAnother catch: does the interp small model actually build a rotating MPC map with 2 masters? route=\"interpolated\" → InterpolatedBeamShellMPCElement with weights [0.6, 0.4] → get_nonlinear_mpc_descriptor → map with 2-master entries. And kinematics=\"corotational\" builds the rotating map. Yes (R3 test uses routes param probably including interpolated).\n\nTest assertions for domain refusal:\n- no exception propagates (the core regression).\n- failure_reason == \"trial_state_domain_refused\".\n- displacements all zero.\n- factorize calls bounded (<= 20).\n- info[\"displacement_control_adaptation\"][\"cutbacks\"] == 8? Assert <= 8 and >= 1. Hmm — with cutbacks reaching max 8 → stop. Actually cutbacks_this_step < max_control_cutbacks (8) required to subdivide → after 8 cutbacks... wait: cutbacks_this_step starts 0; subdivision requires cutbacks_this_step < 8 →